From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: kindle3: always enable the USB recovery console

The upstream environment only starts usbserial when the five-way select GPIO
is asserted during Barebox initialization, and then allows autoboot after 60
seconds. That makes an early RAM-boot failure indistinguishable from a missed
button sample.

Always register the USB serial gadget for the Paper Linux development image.
The board code separately sets the autoboot state through Barebox's C API.

Upstream: Not submitted (development-image policy)
Signed-off-by: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
---
 arch/arm/boards/kindle3/env/init/usbconsole | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boards/kindle3/env/init/usbconsole
+++ b/arch/arm/boards/kindle3/env/init/usbconsole
@@ -1,8 +1,6 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
-# Fiveway device select key activates usbserial access for 60s
+# The RAM-boot development image always exposes its recovery console and waits
+# without requiring the five-way select button.
 echo
-if gpio_get_value 63; then
-	usbserial
-	global.autoboot_timeout=60
-fi
+usbserial
-- 
